From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: RoGetParameterizedTypeInstanceIID computes the IIDs of parameterized types

RoGetParameterizedTypeInstanceIID was a stub that returned E_NOTIMPL and
GUID_NULL, and RoFreeParameterizedTypeExtra and
RoParameterizedTypeExtraGetTypeSignature were not exported. Language
projections (C++/WinRT, .NET CsWinRT, Python and JavaScript bridges) call it
to find the IID of an instance such as IAsyncOperation<Boolean> or
IVector<String> before QueryInterface, so WinRT calls through them failed.

As the WinRT type system defines it, the IID is a name-based (version 5,
SHA-1) UUID made in the namespace 11f47ad5-7b73-42c0-abae-878b1e16adee from
the type's UTF-8 signature:

- fundamental types (b1, c2, i1..u8, f4, f8, g16, string, and
  cinterface(IInspectable) for Object) need no metadata;
- everything else is described by the caller's IRoMetaDataLocator through
  an IRoSimpleMetaDataBuilder: interfaces ({iid}), delegates
  (delegate({iid})), runtime classes and interface groups (rc(Name;default)
  and ig(Name;default), the default interface by IID, by name, or
  parameterized), structs (struct(Name;fields...)), enums (enum(Name;i4) or
  u4 for flags) and parameterized interfaces and delegates
  (pinterface({piid};args...)), whose type arguments are the following name
  elements, as many as the name's `N says;
- a locator that describes a type twice, an unknown type, or the wrong
  number of type arguments make the call fail with GUID_NULL.

The extra handle keeps the signature for
RoParameterizedTypeExtraGetTypeSignature until RoFreeParameterizedTypeExtra.
roparameterizediid.h declares the three functions.

Wine's combase tests: a new test (IAsyncOperation<Boolean>,
IReference<Point>, an unknown type) passes; no other change.

Gate: test/pinterfaceiid-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit: sixteen instances
compared with the IIDs in the SDK headers, the signature, errors). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_STRUCT_FIELDS, SG_MUTANT_NO_UUID_VERSION (combase/roapi.c).
